  <title>SET PRINTER Command</title>
  <keywords>
    <keyword>Commands</keyword>
    <keyword>SET commands</keyword>
    <keyword>SET PRINTER command</keyword>
  </keywords>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET PRINTER Command</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Directs the output of the console commands to the printer, in addition to the screen.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET PRINTER ON | OFF | &amp;&lt;cMacro&gt;</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ON | OFF<tab />ON sends the output also to the printer. OFF stops this. The value may also be a macro (&amp;) that evaluates to ON or OFF.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">The command only changes the Set.Printer setting of the runtime. The variant SET PRINTER TO &lt;file&gt; is not supported at this moment.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibRT" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="Command_SET_CONSOLE">SET CONSOLE</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_MARGIN">SET MARGIN</link></para>
  </body>
</topic>
